      ],
      "text": "5.1. Treatment shortening in children and",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 19.0,
      "type": "heading_main"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        87.472900390625,
        340.8902893066406,
        112.26789855957031
      ],
      "text": "adolescents with non-severe TB",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 19.0,
      "type": "heading_main"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        77.66929626464844,
        126.83843231201172,
        168.3994903564453,
        141.1934356689453
      ],
      "text": "Recommendation:",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        77.66929626464844,
        143.2003936767578,
        519.586669921875,
        157.6433868408203
      ],
      "text": "In children and adolescents between 3 months and 16 years of age with non-severe TB (without",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        77.66929626464844,
        155.2003936767578,
        498.3885192871094,
        169.6433868408203
      ],
      "text": "suspicion or evidence of MDR/RR-TB), a 4-month treatment regimen (2HRZ(E)/2HR) should",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        77.66929626464844,
        167.2003936767578,
        116.70680236816406,
        181.6433868408203
      ],
      "text": "be used.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        77.66929626464844,
        180.6584014892578,
        338.0942687988281,
        197.8404083251953
      ],
      "text": "(Strong recommendation, moderate certainty of evidence)",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        77.66929626464844,
        205.26373291015625,
        120.14249420166016,
        219.6187286376953
      ],
      "text": "Remarks",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        77.66929626464844,
        221.62574768066406,
        510.9369201660156,
        236.06874084472656
      ],
      "text": "•\tNon-severe TB is defined as: Peripheral lymph node TB; intrathoracic lymph node TB without",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        83.66929626464844,
        233.62574768066406,
        512.4702758789062,
        248.06874084472656
      ],
      "text": "airway obstruction; uncomplicated TB pleural effusion or paucibacillary, non-cavitary disease,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        83.66929626464844,
        245.62574768066406,
        377.5882873535156,
        260.0687561035156
      ],
      "text": "confined to one lobe of the lungs, and without a miliary pattern.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        77.66929626464844,
        261.87762451171875,
        508.11541748046875,
        276.3206481933594
      ],
      "text": "•\tChildren and adolescents who do not meet the criteria for non-severe TB should receive the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        83.66929626464844,
        273.87762451171875,
        506.0417785644531,
        288.3206481933594
      ],
      "text": "standard six-month treatment regimen (2HRZE/4HR), or recommended treatment regimens",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        83.66929626464844,
        285.87762451171875,
        262.60888671875,
        300.3206481933594
      ],
      "text": "for severe forms of extrapulmonary TB.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        77.66929626464844,
        302.12957763671875,
        515.2048950195312,
        316.5726013183594
      ],
      "text": "•\tThe use of ethambutol in the first two months of treatment is recommended in settings with a",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        83.66929626464844,
        314.12957763671875,
        319.8359069824219,
        328.5726013183594
      ],
      "text": "high prevalence of HIV,  or of isoniazid resistance. 26 27",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        356.8479919433594,
        298.9844970703125,
        377.7279968261719
      ],
      "text": "5.1.1. Justification and evidence",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 16.0,
      "type": "heading_main"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        383.9319152832031,
        527.543701171875,
        398.37493896484375
      ],
      "text": "The majority of children with TB have less severe forms of the disease than adults. Treatment regimens",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.97652530670166,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        397.13189697265625,
        527.4585571289062,
        411.5749206542969
      ],
      "text": "that are shorter than those for adults may be effective in treating children with TB, however solid",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        410.3319091796875,
        527.55810546875,
        424.7749328613281
      ],
      "text": "evidence to substantiate this has been lacking to date. Shorter treatment regimens can result in lower",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.985940933227539,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        423.5318908691406,
        527.4244384765625,
        437.97491455078125
      ],
      "text": "costs to families and health services, potentially less toxicity, lower risks of drug-drug interactions in",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        436.7319030761719,
        527.4102783203125,
        451.1749267578125
      ],
      "text": "children living with HIV, and fewer problems with adherence. Shorter, safe and effective treatment",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        449.9319152832031,
        527.5390014648438,
        464.37493896484375
      ],
      "text": "regimens for children with both drug-susceptible and DR-TB benefit children with TB and their families,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.95761775970459,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        463.13189697265625,
        527.5526733398438,
        477.5749206542969
      ],
      "text": "and are a key intervention to achieve the End TB Strategy targets, as well as targets related to children",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.977978706359863,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        476.3319091796875,
        527.435546875,
        490.7749328613281
      ],
      "text": "set during the UNGA High-Level Meeting on the fight against tuberculosis in 2018. New evidence",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        489.5318908691406,
        527.4036865234375,
        503.97491455078125
      ],
      "text": "from a recently completed trial on the shortened treatment of drug-susceptible TB in children and",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        502.73193359375,
        503.74591064453125,
        517.1749267578125
      ],
      "text": "adolescents has paved the way for new recommendations on shorter regimens for this group.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        524.435791015625,
        527.4179077148438,
        538.8787841796875
      ],
      "text": "The SHINE trial (Shorter Treatment for Minimal Tuberculosis in Children) was the first and only large",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        537.6358642578125,
        527.3178100585938,
        552.078857421875
      ],
      "text": "phase three trial to evaluate the duration of TB treatment in children with non-severe drug-susceptible",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.967501640319824,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        550.8359375,
        527.4157104492188,
        565.2789306640625
      ],
      "text": "TB. Therefore, evidence from the trial rather than a systematic review, was used to answer this",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        561.2418823242188,
        527.3897705078125,
        578.4788818359375
      ],
      "text": "(57) PICO question  . The SHINE trial was a multi-centre, open-label, parallel-group, non-inferiority,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        577.23583984375,
        527.4134521484375,
        591.6788330078125
      ],
      "text": "randomized, controlled, two-arm trial comparing 4-month (16 weeks) versus the standard 6-month",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        590.435791015625,
        527.1990356445312,
        604.8787841796875
      ],
      "text": "(24 weeks) treatment durations in children under 16 years of age with symptomatic non-severe",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        603.6359252929688,
        527.3858642578125,
        618.0789184570312
      ],
      "text": "TB. Children and young adolescents aged below 16 years were treated with rifampicin, isoniazid,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        616.8359375,
        527.5791625976562,
        631.2789306640625
      ],
      "text": "pyrazinamide with or without ethambutol using WHO recommended doses, appropriate for paediatric",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.957366943359375,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        627.2418823242188,
        127.12730407714844,
        644.4788818359375
      ],
      "text": "(58) dosing  .",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        651.5638427734375,
        527.5756225585938,
        666.1828002929688
      ],
      "text": "PICO question:  In children and adolescents with non-severe TB, should a 4-month intervention",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiboldItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        664.9398193359375,
        476.201416015625,
        679.3828125
      ],
      "text": "regimen versus the standard 6-month regimen conforming to WHO guidelines be used?",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        718.2371215820312,
        526.598388671875,
        731.9411010742188
      ],
      "text": "Defined as countries, subnational administrative units, or selected facilities, where the HIV prevalence among adult pregnant women is  26",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        81.86609649658203,
        729.005126953125,
        526.5993041992188,
        741.5410766601562
      ],
      "text": "Guidance for national tuberculosis programmes on the management of tuberculosis in  ≥1% or among TB patients is ≥5% in the 2014",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        81.86609649658203,
        738.6051635742188,
        174.0366973876953,
        751.14111328125
      ],
      "text": "children (second edition) (8) .",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        749.871826171875,
        526.570556640625,
        763.5758056640625
      ],
      "text": "WHO does not intend to establish thresholds for low, moderate or high levels of prevalence of isoniazid resistance; NTPs will establish  27",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        81.86609649658203,
        762.6718139648438,
        195.48350524902344,
        773.17578125
      ],
      "text": "definitions for their own countries.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
